<header><p class="st-kicker">imperial city · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Free Imperial City of Pfullendorf</h1><p class="st-meta">1220 CE – 1803 CE (approx.) · capital Pfullendorf</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Small Swabian imperial city north of Lake Constance, chartered by Frederick II in 1220 and a modest Catholic member of the Swabian city leagues.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Pfullendorf was the seat of counts whose lands passed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hohenstaufen">Hohenstaufen</a> in the later 12th century. In 1220 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-ii">Emperor Frederick II</a> granted the town its charter, and it became an imperial city on the roads between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-constance">Lake Constance</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The town was governed by a council with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guild">guild</a> participation and lived from linen weaving, crafts and its market for the surrounding countryside. Its small territory included a few villages. It joined the Swabian city leagues and later the Swabian imperial circle, but remained a minor power, and it stayed Catholic during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Pfullendorf lost its imperial freedom in 1803 when it was annexed by the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/margraviate-of-baden">Margraviate of Baden</a>, soon the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/grand-duchy-of-baden">Grand Duchy of Baden</a>. It is now a small town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baden-wurttemberg">Baden-Württemberg</a> with a well-preserved old centre and parts of its medieval walls.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="imperial city, 1220 CE – 1803 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V42 H32 V34 H40 V42 H46 V34 H54 V42 H60 V34 H68 V42 H76 V82 Z"/><path d="M44 82 V66 Q50 58 56 66 V82"/><path d="M34 54 H40 M60 54 H66"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">imperial city</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Germany and Central Europe</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:83.98%;width:11.60%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1220 CE – 1803 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>imperial city</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Pfullendorf</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Swabian German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Pfullendorf</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1512&amp;focus=free-imperial-city-of-pfullendorf" aria-label="Free Imperial City of Pfullendorf on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4896 500 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Free Imperial City of Pfullendorf lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5216 756L5229 694M5216 756L5194 723"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5229 694h0M5194 723h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5216 756h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5216 756h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Pfullendorf. <a href="/atlas?year=1512&amp;focus=free-imperial-city-of-pfullendorf">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
